    "notes": [
      "Estimación directa simplificada: 5% of net profit is deducted as hard-to-justify expenses, up to EUR 2,000 (art. 30 RIRPF). In estimación directa normal there is no such deduction; the estimate is then slightly low. Estimación objetiva (módulos) does not apply to professional services.",
      "IRPF is the state scale plus the scale of the community where you lived most of the year; Navarra and the Basque Country apply their own foral IRPF. The reduction for low business income (art. 32.2 LIRPF) and family minimums are not included.",
      "RETA is paid monthly by direct debit, outside the vault, unless the reserve is meant to cover it; the estimate deducts it from profit before IRPF."
    ],
